the same recovery words + passphrase show the same fingerprint.
a different passphrase opens a different wallet.
compare this code with your coordinator.␀␀␀tap the KISS logo any time to go back to the game.␀␀WHERE SHOULD THIS WALLET LIVE?␀␀asked again whenever you set up a wallet␀␀␀␀KEEP ON THIS DEVICE␀the words stay on here. unlock with just your passphrase.␀␀␀NOTHING SAVED␀␀␀load your words every time you use it. nothing on here to find.␀LOAD YOUR WALLET␀␀␀␀nothing is saved on this device␀SCAN A SEED QR␀␀a seed QR you already made on another signer. this device never makes one.␀␀NOT A SEED␀␀nothing was loaded␀␀that QR is not a seed this device
understands, or a word is wrong.

nothing changed. try again.␀TRY AGAIN␀␀␀PASSPHRASE FROM A QR␀␀␀␀read this first␀whoever can read that QR can open
this wallet.

a photo of it is the same as the QR.

the scan is used exactly as printed.␀␀SCAN IT␀type the words from your paper.␀ERASE THE SEED?␀the words go from this device now.

only your paper + passphrase can
bring this wallet back.␀␀␀␀HOLD TO ERASE␀␀␀FULL BACKUP NOT VERIFIED␀␀␀␀FULL BACKUP VERIFIED␀␀␀␀TYPE THE EXACT BACKUP PASSPHRASE␀␀␀␀THAT OPENS A DIFFERENT WALLET. TRY AGAIN.␀␀␀TOTAL LEAVING WALLET␀␀␀␀unsigned first, then A-Z. signed files are labelled.␀␀␀␀UNSIGNED␀␀␀␀SIMPLE EXPLAINERS␀␀␀INPUTS: coins this transaction spends.
OUTPUTS: every place the transaction sends bitcoin.
CHANGE: the part returned to an address KISS verified as yours.
TXID: the tracking ID used after broadcast.
FEE RATE: fee paid for each unit of transaction size.
LOCKTIME: the earliest block where it may confirm.
DERIVATION PATH: the standard branch used to find a key.
DESCRIPTOR: a read-only map that can watch and find addresses, but cannot spend.␀␀␀NOT FOUND IN FIRST %u ADDRESSES␀valid for this network, but outside the first 100 receiving/change addresses searched. this is not definitive.␀␀WRONG NETWORK␀␀␀this address is valid, but for the other Bitcoin network. switch networks or scan again.␀␀␀␀INVALID ADDRESS␀the address format or checksum is invalid. do not use it.␀␀␀Looking for the QR code␀point the camera at the screen showing it␀␀␀Found it: hold steady␀␀␀Too much packed into this QR␀␀␀␀ask your coordinator for an animated QR␀Move back a little␀␀part of the code is out of view␀Reading␀Point at something with detail␀␀books, a plant, your desk: not a blank wall␀Looking good: tap to capture␀␀␀␀the photo mixes with chip randomness to make your words␀x close␀of␀␀STORAGE␀COORDINATOR WATCHES + CREATES THE PSBT␀␀KISS CHECKS + SIGNS THE PSBT␀␀␀␀COORDINATOR BROADCASTS THE TRANSACTION␀␀WHAT IS A SEED?␀YOUR SEED PHRASE␀␀␀␀12 or 24 ordered words, called a BIP39 mnemonic␀those words plus your passphrase are what make your wallet. not this device.

write both down and any compatible BIP39 signer or wallet app can rebuild it, even if this device is lost.

the words alone rebuild a different wallet: the one with no passphrase.␀␀␀UNDERLINE␀␀␀LINE ABOVE␀␀LINE THROUGH␀␀␀␀CIRCLE IT␀␀␀TICK␀␀␀␀TWO WAYS IN␀one opens your wallet. one opens a wallet you can afford to show.␀␀␀drawing KISS opens a spare wallet with no passphrase asked for.

add one more stroke after the word and it asks for your passphrase and opens your real wallet instead.

nobody watching can tell the spare from the only one.␀␀PUT A LITTLE IN THE SPARE␀␀␀the spare wallet has its own fingerprint and really works.

send a small amount to it. an empty wallet on a signer looks like a wallet somebody is hiding something behind.␀YOUR STROKE␀draw KISS, then this, to reach your real wallet␀DRAW IT␀draw your stroke on the word below␀␀ONCE MORE␀␀␀the same stroke again, so a slip now does not lock you out later␀␀␀␀THAT WAS NOT IT␀nothing was saved.

try the stroke again, or go back
and pick a different one.␀␀NOT NOW␀BOTH WAYS IN ARE SET␀␀␀␀KISS on its own opens the spare wallet.

KISS with your stroke asks for your passphrase and opens your real one.

you can change this later from SETTINGS, inside your real wallet.␀which stroke opens which wallet.␀␀␀␀NOT SET␀TURN THIS OFF␀␀␀no passphrase: your words alone open this wallet␀␀␀␀a passphrase added later opens a different wallet␀␀␀THIS WALLET HAS NO PASSPHRASE␀␀␀your words alone open it. anyone who reads
them can spend from it.

a passphrase added later opens a DIFFERENT
wallet: it cannot protect this one.

know this one by its fingerprint:␀␀␀NOTHING TO HIDE BEHIND␀␀a spare wallet only works if your real one has a passphrase. this one has none, so every way in opens it.

to use this, make a wallet with a passphrase and move your coins there.␀␀REPLACE THE SEED?␀␀␀finishing this makes a new seed and the one on this device now is replaced.

your paper + passphrase still open the old wallet. nothing changes until you finish.␀␀␀MAKE A NEW SEED␀psbtÿ␀␀␀cHNidP␀␀p%dof%d␀crypto-psbt␀p%dof%d %.*s␀␀␀␀/sdcard␀.psbt␀␀␀%s/%s␀␀␀rb␀␀wb␀␀camspike␀␀␀␀W (%lu) %s: scan: sensor has no exposure control
